        "section": [
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">COPD exacerbation, treated with bronchodilators and steroids</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
                {
                  "code": "67781-5",
                  "system": "http://loinc.org",
                  "display": "Summarization of encounter note"
                }
              ]
            },
            "title": "Synthesis"
          },
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the hospital course of your 73-year-old male patient, admitted on 16/08/2019 due to an acute exacerbation of his known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease (COPD). On admission, physical examination revealed reduced air entry bilaterally with expiratory wheezing. Oxygen saturation was diminished at room air. Diagnostic workup included arterial blood gas analysis confirming hypercapnic respiratory failure, chest X-ray showing pulmonary hyperinflation without consolidation, and blood tests revealing mild inflammatory changes. The patient was treated with nebulised bronchodilators, systemic corticosteroids, supplemental oxygen therapy, and close monitoring of vital signs and pulse oximetry. He responded well to treatment with significant symptomatic improvement. He was discharged stable on 17/08/2019 with optimised inhaler therapy and outpatient pulmonary follow-up arranged. Please continue chronic disease monitoring and consider pulmonary rehabilitation referral.</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
                {
                  "code": "8648-8",
                  "system": "http://loinc.org",
                  "display": "Hospital course note"
